# LiteLLM Metadata-Only Integration Prototype

This example shows a LiteLLM integration where Hokusai receives routing metadata
and contribution rows only. Raw prompts, message content, tool arguments, and
completion text stay in the LiteLLM/provider path.

## Quickstart

```sh
cd examples/litellm-integration
python3 -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e '.[dev]'
ruff check .
mypy hokusai_litellm
pytest -q
python examples/run_demo.py
```

Set `HOKUSAI_API_KEY` and `HOKUSAI_API_BASE_URL` to point at a live backend.
The demo runs against local mocks by default.

## Privacy boundary

- Hokusai routing requests are built from an allowlisted metadata payload only.
- Contribution rows use `harness_outcome_row/v1` and exclude prompt/message
  fields by schema and by explicit forbidden-key checks.
- This is not a Hokusai prompt proxy. See [../../docs/litellm-integration.md](../../docs/litellm-integration.md).
